<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Army of Vietnam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PAVN, Vietnam People's Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> is the armed force of Vietnam, founded in December 1944 as a small propaganda unit under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vo-nguyen-giap">Vo Nguyen Giap</a>. It fought the French in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war">First Indochina War</a>, winning at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954, and defeated South Vietnam and its American allies by 1975. It then invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> in 1978 and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1979.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-army-of-vietnam.jpg" alt="People's Army of Vietnam" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sshu94, updated by Hwipadam. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_VPA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>People’s Army of Vietnam</b> emerged from the war against the United States as one of the largest and most experienced armies in the world, and the new state used it almost at once.</blockquote><a href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Socialist Republic of Vietnam · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The first major battle between the United States Army and the <b>People's Army of Vietnam</b> began at the foot of the Chu Pong Massif.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-14">14 November in history</a></li></ul></section>
